      ":question/id": "41a25d24-92e3-5f69-a48f-6721c965257d",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry $a_{22}=9$ is in the same column as the leading entry $a_{12}=-9$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -9 & 6 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -8 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry $b_{22}=-4$ is in the same column as the leading entry $b_{12}=-1$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are **not** in row echelon form.",
