    "question": {
      ":question/id": "31b4c00a-8c14-513f-aca9-bcded71a34c9",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry $a_{32}=-9$ is to the left of the leading entry $a_{23}=-7$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry $c_{32}=1$ is to the left of the leading entry $c_{23}=-2$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form.",
